A ruthless Seeker with a hidden agenda, Rassimov joined [[the Organization]] and quickly established himself as [[the Professor]]'s perfect operative, with over a hundred missions and no failures. {{source|The Unseen Guide}} This was, however, all part of a much bigger plans to prevent the Professor from becoming too powerful and eventually causing his downfall. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}
[[File:S1E18 Darkvoid Rassimov Cavalier.jpg|thumb|170px|Rassimov uses his devastating [[Darkvoid]] power to destroy [[Cavalier]]]]

He had his first direct encounter with the Huntik team at the [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot]] where he tailed [[Dante Vale]] and [[Lok Lambert]], helping them survive several of the deadly tests so that they would lead him to [[Sir Lancelot]]'s Titan [[Cavalier]]. As him and his [[Suits]] attacked, he easily defeated Lok and claimed the Amulet. However, the noble Titan refused to bond with him, so Rassimov callously destroyed the Titan using his devastating [[Darkvoid]] power, to the horror of the Huntik team. {{source|Memory Lane}}

Based on his intense hatred for the Casterwills, the Foundation suspected him to be connected to the [[Nullifiers]] whom Casterwill defeated. He was extremely physically skilled and possessed a command of dark spells and Titans, making him a match for [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] whole team. {{source|The Unseen Guide}} After following the team to [[Atlantis]], Rassimov fought with an enraged Lok who blamed the Organization for causing him to lose his father, believing him to be dead. Using all his strength, Lok managed to defeat Rassimov, forcing him and his men to retreat. {{source|Coming of Age}}

After appearing to fall into one of his own traps, he gave [[Dante Vale]] the Amulet of [[Archwarder]] so that the team could use it to defeat the Professor. He then met up with his real group, the [[Blood Spiral]], and plotted the end of the world and the [[Casterwill family]], with [[Shauna]] and [[Wind]]. {{source|The Divine Comedy}} 

[[File:S2E32_Rassimov_Darkvoid.png|thumb|170px|Rassimov returns]]
After the Professor´s defeat, Rassimov made his return in [[Klaus' bookshop]], revealing himself as the leader of the Blood Spirals. He attempted to eliminate Dante but was stopped when the latter [[powerbonded]] with [[Caliban]]. He and his forces then left with the [[Amulet]] of [[Void]] but not before completely destroying the lab. {{source|The Blood Spiral}} 

Rassimov began searching for new members for the Brotherhood and sent his minions to hunt the Casterwill family, while he talked with the Betrayer on his throne. He ordained several of [[Tantras]]' orphan recruits including the brothers [[Den]] and [[Harrison Fears]] with the tattoo of Blood Spiral. {{source|Den vs Harrison}} {{source|Zhalia's Mission}} {{Source|Sophie on Trial}} 

Rassimov traveled to the [[Tomb of Tutankhamun]] in [[Egypt]] with [[Harrison Fears]] to recover the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]]. He was then ambushed and arrested by the [[Huntik Foundation]] his [[Amulets]] all unbonded and locked away by [[Dante]] and his [[Sorrowbond]] power. However he was rescued by Harrison and, revealing the true extent of his power, summoned the [[Legendary Titan]] of War, [[Legion]]. Defeating the Huntik team, and destroying the Amulets of [[Lindorm]] and [[Solwing]], Rassimov escaped with the Necklace. {{source|Rassimov's Secret}} The team took time to recover from this defeat, staying at the [[Lambert house]] in [[County Kerry, Ireland]]. {{source|Back Home}}

[[File:S2E50 Rassimov Void Comet.png|thumb|170px|Rassimov and [[Void]] attempt to control the [[Red Comet]]]]
On the longest night of the year, Rassimov prepared the ritual to activate the [[Spiral Mark]] by summoning the [[Nullifier]] scout, [[Void]]. {{source|Words from Eathon}} When Dante and his team arrived, Rassimov announced he would deal with them personally, summoning Legion. However he was defeated by Dante and Legion destroyed by Lok and the [[Willblade]]. Following the revelation that the [[Red Comet]] had changed course to hit the spot of the Spiral Mark, Rassimov revealed his own scheme to double cross the Betrayer and the other Spirals, planning to control the Nullifiers with the Necklace of Tutankhamun. However, his plan failed when the Necklace was disintegrated and he died in the subsequent collision with the Comet. {{source|The Spiral Mark}}

